    "method": [
     "Super-grid 1/48 deg (1.25'), node-registered, H=8641 W=17281.",
     "Land = ne_10m_land OR ne_10m_minor_islands OR ne_10m_antarctic_ice_shelves_polys, then AND-NOT ne_10m_lakes (holes of lake polygons stay land). Each polygon part is drawn with Pillow ImageDraw.polygon on its own bounding-box canvas (exterior ring = 1, then its holes = 0) and ORed (lakes: AND-NOT) into the global layer.",
     "Pixel transform: u = (lon+180)*48, v = (90-lat)*48 (node units); canvas x_px = 4*(u-j0)+0.5, y_px = 4*(v-i0)+0.5, sampled at every 4th pixel, so canvas pixel (4*a, 4*b) is centred on node (i0+a, j0+b). Pillow truncates vertices to int and fills closed spans; the 4x canvas confines that to nodes within ~1/4 node of an edge (self_test).",
     "Seam: column 0 and column W-1 := column 0 OR column W-1 (lake ids: first non-zero).",
     "Lake ids: same rasterization; lowest feature index wins where lake polygons overlap (mostly Great Lakes bay features such as Georgian Bay inside Lake Huron, which thus keep few or no nodes).",
     "SDF: land raster wrap-padded by 1536 columns per side (in 4 longitude tiles; padding grown until every distance < pad, so the wrap is exact), scipy.ndimage.distance_transform_edt on land and on water, sdf_px = edt_land - 0.5 on land, -(edt_water - 0.5) on water, cropped, times 2.316561 km (meridional 1/48 deg, R = 6371.0 km).",
     "5' grid: every 4th super-grid node (exact node correspondence), enforce_seam."
    ],
    "approximations": [
     "Distances are measured in the lat/lon pixel grid: east-west distances are overestimated by 1/cos(latitude) (no wrap over the poles).",
     "Quantised to the 1.25' super-grid: the coastline sits midway between land and water nodes, so |sdf| >= 0.5 super-pixel (1.16 km) and errors up to about one super-pixel.",
     "Vertices snap to 1/4 super-node and spans are closed, so nodes within ~1/4 super-node (~0.6 km) of an edge may differ from an exact point-in-polygon test; boundary nodes on lat -90 and lon +-180 edges count as inside.",
     "Features narrower than the 5' node spacing can be missed by the node sampling.",
     "The Caspian Sea is a hole of the ne_10m_land polygon, not an ne_10m_lakes feature, so it is water with lake_id 0.",
     "ne_10m_land feature 'Null island' (fictitious 0.009 deg square at 0N 0E) excluded."
    ]
   }
